module iam

# ========================================
# PLATFORM CLIENT TYPE (Organization-scoped)
# ========================================
# OAuth2 client credentials for platform builders embedding Stigmer
# into their products. Holds client_id + client_secret_hash for
# inbound authentication via the mintUserToken RPC.
# Scoped to organization — each platform client is owned by an org.
#
# Access model: RESTRICTED, managed by the organization's current admins
# Platform clients contain sensitive credential material (client_secret_hash)
# and mint tokens for the organization's product users, so they are the
# organization's credential, not a person's. Plain members and viewer-role
# members of the organization see nothing. `owner` is computed, never
# stored: it is the organization's admins, as an identity provider is
# managed, so a client stays manageable whoever created it, and a creator
# who is demoted below admin or removed loses control of it with the role.
# Rotating a secret hands out a credential that mints into the
# organization, so that control must end when the role that granted it
# does. The creator is recorded in the audit trail (kind_meta `owner_type`
# NONE). Public visibility is intentionally unsupported to prevent
# credential leakage.
#
# Permission pattern:
# - Org Admin (and org owner, through admin): full management, secret
#   rotation included. The plaintext secret and hash are never returned by
#   the API layer.
# - Direct viewer grant: can see the client and who has access to it
# - Org Members and Viewers: no access (administrative resource)
#
# FGA tuple on creation (the kind's creation event: organization scope, no
# owner; private, so no visibility tuple):
# - platform_client:pcl_abc#organization@organization:acme
#
# Checks the handlers make: `can_create_platform_client` on the
# organization to create; `can_view` to get, get by reference, and to keep
# a row in the organization's list; `can_edit` to update and to rotate the
# secret; `can_delete` to delete. Minting authenticates the client by its
# credentials and asks nothing of this type.

type platform_client
  relations
    # ========================================
    # PARENT ORGANIZATION
    # ========================================
    define organization: [organization]
    
    # ========================================
    # OWNERSHIP
    # ========================================
    # Every current admin of the client's organization, and nobody else.
    define owner: admin from organization
    
    # ========================================
    # VIEWER ACCESS
    # ========================================
    # Owners (admins included) and direct viewer grants. Organization
    # members and viewers are deliberately absent.
    define viewer: [identity_account] or owner
    
    # ========================================
    # PERMISSIONS
    # ========================================
    define can_view: viewer
    define can_edit: owner
    define can_delete: owner
    
    # ========================================
    # IAM POLICY MANAGEMENT
    # ========================================
    define can_grant_access: owner
    define can_view_access: viewer
